e exchange factor 2/Rap GEF2</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.00</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">IPI00853219</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">34</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Ras GTPase-activating protein/SynGap</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">17</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.00</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">IPI00177884</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">35</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">R-type calcium channel</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.00</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">IPI00218338</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">36</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Voltage-dependent anion-selective channel</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">21</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.00</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">IPI00216024</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="nt101"><p>Peptide identifications were confirmed by inspection of MS2 spectra and targeted MS2 analysis of peptide parent masses. Description: IPI identifier. &#x00025; Cov: Percent of protein sequence covered by observed peptides. Peptides reported here have also been observed in at least three other analyses of mammalian PSD preparations as described in Colins et al <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="pone.0005251-Collins1">&#x0005b;39&#x0005d;</xref>.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="pone-0005251-t002" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0005251.t002</object-id><label>Table 2</label><caption><title>Subject Information.</title></caption><graphic id="pone-0005251-t002-2" xlink:href="pone.0005251.t002"/><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" alternate-form-of="pone-0005251-t002-2"><colgroup span="1"><col align="left" span="1"/><col align="c